---
import SectionHeader from "@/components/ui/SectionHeader.astro";
import TabLabel from "@/components/ui/TabLabel.astro";
---

<section class="py-16 md:py-24">
  <input checked class="sr-only" id="tab-intro" name="story-tabs" type="radio" />
  <input class="sr-only" id="tab-background" name="story-tabs" type="radio" />

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-12">
      <SectionHeader title="The story" navClass="story-tabs">
        <TabLabel for="tab-intro" label="Intro" />
        <TabLabel for="tab-background" label="Background" />
      </SectionHeader>
    </div>

    <div class="lg:col-span-9 lg:col-start-4 max-w-3xl story-content">
      <div class="tab-content space-y-8" id="content-intro">
        <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-light leading-relaxed text-(--foreground)/90">
          I'm a software engineer who builds <span class="font-normal">reliable systems</span>. Most
          of my time goes into backend architecture, infrastructure and the day-to-day operations
          that let a company grow without things falling over.
        </p>
        <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-light leading-relaxed text-(--foreground)/90">
          I'm based in <span class="font-normal">Amsterdam</span>, where I'm a founding engineer at
          <span class="font-normal">Coolset</span>, helping grow the engineering team and the
          infrastructure under it. The work I enjoy most sits between code, product and the
          business. I like owning a problem from the first conversation through to production.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tab-content space-y-8" id="content-background">
        <div class="font-light">
          <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed text-lg text-(--foreground)/80">
            I started coding at school in Johannesburg. I picked information technology there and
            electrical and computer engineering at university. Both were educated guesses that
            turned out to be the right ones. Engineering let me point my love of maths and puzzles
            at real problems.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed text-lg text-(--foreground)/80">
            Software won me over because you can turn an idea into something useful quickly. I get
            the most out of automating tedious work. Even better is when something people used to
            complain about becomes something they stop noticing.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed text-lg text-(--foreground)/80">
            A lot of the job is people. A new system only works if the team using it trusts it.
            That's why I spend time listening to what each team actually needs and explaining the
            trade-offs in plain terms.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-lg text-(--foreground)/80">
            Being observant has become central to how I work. I notice where a process keeps
            breaking or where a small detail causes friction every day. Fixing those consistently is
            most of what makes a system last.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
